commit 0e4c63a3a69787325df0ca6f4722198e549e15e8
Author: ledger <ledger@example.invalid>
Date:   Mon Nov 23 01:58:22 2026 +0000

    Add a tasks board for the committee
    
    The task sheet goes on a board like the events one, so the Thursday meeting
    stops being a read-through (minutes 12 Nov). Layout follows what the
    committee asked for:
    - one section per person, so each person sees what is theirs (Ines);
    - tasks with nobody's name on them come first, since that is how the water
      meter and the shed gutter sat untouched;
    - done tasks folded away at the bottom (Tomas);
    - due dates flagged overdue / this week;
    - the polytunnel rota at the top, from this week on, blank weeks shown as
      "nobody yet" (Dot, and the September swap mix-up).
    
    kit/board.py gains opt-in board.json settings for this (undated sections,
    row sort, done fold, rota, date and prefix columns). Boards that don't set
    them build exactly as before: the events page is byte-identical.
    Names and statuses are matched ignoring case ("priya", "Done" in the
    export), so the next export works without hand-fixing the CSV.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

